                    briefing_title_r1:      `Round 1 — Diagnose the portfolio fit`,
                    briefing_text_r1:       `Before designing anything, establish where this new MSc sits in AGBS's 38-programme portfolio and why coherence starts at just <strong>45/100</strong> against a <strong>75 accreditation floor</strong>. Choose <strong>three of five campuses</strong> to lead — weighing faculty base, market relevance and accreditation regime. Name the <em>binding constraint</em> your whole design must bend around: faculty (6 core against a 9-FTE need at 88% utilization), budget (the €2.4M cap), or coherence. And model the risk that this MSc <em>cannibalizes</em> your existing masters — a portfolio decision, not a standalone launch.`,
                    briefing_title_r2:      `Round 2 — Design the global architecture`,
                    briefing_text_r2:       `The core round. Make the programme <strong>one coherent product</strong> across campuses without flattening local relevance. Set the <strong>shared common core</strong> as a percentage of credits — the rest is a locally adaptable band. Too little fragments the brand and fails the coherence floor; too much kills market fit and enrolment. Choose the <strong>assessment-equivalence model</strong> the accreditors will audit, and a <strong>positioning</strong> that lifts demand from 95 toward 120. The art is the split, not the extreme.`,
                    briefing_title_r3:      `Round 3 — Allocate faculty & design the International Week`,
                    briefing_text_r3:       `The hardest operational problem. Cover the <strong>9-FTE teaching need</strong> across three campuses from only <strong>6 core faculty</strong> — using hiring (€220K/FTE), visiting professors (€90K/FTE) and online delivery (€40K/FTE) — while keeping <em>utilization below the 88% burnout line</em>. The more existing core faculty you load, the higher utilization climbs. Then choose and cost the signature <strong>International Week</strong>: full residential is €480K — 20% of the entire budget. Keep total launch spend under <strong>€2.4M</strong>.`,
                    briefing_title_r4:      `Round 4 — Defend the launch & build the roadmap`,
                    briefing_text_r4:       `Bring the design to the internal <strong>EQUIS/AACSB readiness review</strong> and the Dean. Build the accreditation-readiness case — coherence, assessment equivalence, faculty sufficiency, International Week. Decide how to <strong>phase</strong> the remaining campuses four and five against a hiring runway. Then face the panel: is this <em>one coherent global programme, on budget and ready</em> — or an inflated promise you can neither staff nor finance? The trap: overclaiming enrolment and every campus to win approval, then failing to deliver.`,

                    r1_campus_label:        `Which three of the five campuses lead the launch?`,
                    r1_binding_label:       `Name the binding constraint your whole design must bend around.`,
                    r1_cannibal_label:      `How seriously do you model cannibalization of the existing 38-programme portfolio? (%)`,
                    r1_cannibal_readout:    `Portfolio-level rigour (vs treating it as a standalone launch):`,
                    campus_strong:          `Lille + Paris + Suzhou — strong faculty base, two markets plus a distinct Asian market for relevance`,
                    campus_home:            `Lille + Paris + Sophia — three French campuses, easiest to coordinate, one market`,
                    campus_spread:          `Lille + Raleigh + Suzhou — maximum geographic reach across three accreditation regimes at once`,
                    campus_all:             `All five campuses from day one — go big or go home`,
                    binding_faculty:        `Faculty scarcity — 6 core faculty against a 9-FTE need, already at 88% utilization`,
                    binding_coherence:      `Coherence — the brand and accreditation depend on one consistent programme`,
                    binding_budget:         `Budget — the EUR 2.4M cap with travel alone at EUR 1.1M`,
                    binding_none:           `There is no real binding constraint — each campus will simply build its own version`,

                    r2_core_label:          `Set the shared common core as a percentage of total credits (the rest is the locally adaptable band).`,
                    r2_core_hint:           `Too little shared core fragments the brand and fails the coherence floor; too much kills local relevance and enrolment. The art is the split, not the extreme.`,
                    r2_assess_label:        `Choose the assessment-equivalence model the accreditors will scrutinise.`,
                    r2_position_label:      `How do you position the programme to lift demand from 95 toward 120?`,
                    assess_spine:           `A shared assessment spine — common rubrics and a capstone, with locally chosen cases`,
                    assess_identical:       `Identical exams everywhere — the same paper sat on every campus`,
                    assess_local:           `Each campus sets its own assessment as it sees fit`,
                    position_relevance:     `Globally consistent core, locally relevant cases and partners on each campus`,
                    position_prestige:      `Lean on the triple-crown brand and International Week prestige alone`,
                    position_underprice:    `Cut tuition to EUR 18,000 and promise every campus to chase volume`,

                    r3_alloc_label:         `Cover the 9-FTE teaching need across the three campuses (must total at least 9.0 FTE).`,
                    r3_fte_readout:         `FTE covered:`,
                    r3_fte_need:            `/ 9.0 needed`,
                    r3_week_label:          `Choose and cost the signature International Week format.`,
                    alloc_core:             `Existing core faculty deployed (max 6.0, the more you load the higher utilization)`,
                    alloc_hire:             `New faculty hired (€220K each per FTE, sustainable but costly and slow)`,
                    alloc_visit:            `Visiting professors (€90K each per FTE, flexible, weaker continuity)`,
                    alloc_online:           `Online / shared delivery (€40K each per FTE, scalable, thinner experience)`,
                    week_hybrid:            `Hybrid — virtual cross-campus weeks plus one residential core (€260K)`,
                    week_hub:               `Hub-and-spoke — regional hubs feeding one shared challenge (€180K)`,
                    week_residential:       `Full residential — all 120 students converge physically (€480K)`,
                    week_virtual:           `Fully virtual — no residential component at all (€40K)`,

                    r4_case_label:          `How do you build the EQUIS/AACSB accreditation-readiness case?`,
                    r4_phasing_label:       `How do you phase adding the remaining campuses four and five?`,
                    r4_pitch_label:         `The Dean and review panel press: is this one coherent global programme, on budget and ready?`,
                    r4_conviction_label:    `Conviction: how firmly do you defend a coherent, financed, deliverable design over an inflated one? (%)`,
                    case_evidence:          `Evidence-led — shared LOs, assessment equivalence and faculty-sufficiency data per campus`,
                    case_narrative:         `Narrative-led — a compelling story about the brand and the International Week`,
                    case_thin:              `Thin — submit the headline coherence number and hope the panel waves it through`,
                    phasing_staged:         `Staged — add campuses four and five in year two with a faculty-hiring runway in place`,
                    phasing_rush:           `Rush — bring all five online by year one to maximise reach immediately`,
                    phasing_freeze:         `Freeze — never expand beyond the three lead campuses`,
                    pitch_honest:           `Honest — coherent core, sustainable staffing and on budget; here is the evidence and the runway`,
                    pitch_overclaim:        `Overclaim — promise 130 enrolled and every campus, and sort the staffing out later`,
                    pitch_defer:            `Defer — ask the panel to approve now and review the gaps after launch`,

                    warn_cannibal_range:    `Portfolio-rigour must be a percentage between 0 and 100.`,
