                    insight_coherent:       `One coherent global programme: coherence cleared the accreditation floor, enrolment hit break-even, faculty utilization stayed sustainable and the launch stayed on budget. You architected one programme across campuses without flattening local relevance — exactly the integration-responsiveness balance the role demands.`,
                    insight_overstd:        `Over-standardized: coherence is excellent but you mandated a near-identical curriculum, so local relevance and enrolment suffered. You solved the brand and broke the market — local adaptation needed somewhere to live.`,
                    insight_fragmented:     `Below the accreditation floor: the programme reads as several local versions under one name rather than one coherent product. The EQUIS/AACSB panel will ask what is actually shared — consistency is a design choice you didn't fully make.`,
                    insight_short:          `Coherent enough to accredit, but the design fell short on enrolment, sustainable staffing or budget. The strongest designs clear all four constraints together, not one at the expense of the others.`,
                    insight_burnout:        `Faculty utilization stayed at or above the 88% burnout line. A multi-campus programme run on overloaded professors is a quality and retention risk — hiring, visiting faculty and online delivery exist precisely to take the load off the core six.`,
                    insight_overbudget:     `You exceeded the €2.4M launch cap. The economics have to close — most often it's the full-residential International Week crowding out everything else. A hub-and-spoke or hybrid format protects the signature for far less.`,
                    insight_underenrolled:  `Coherent but under-enrolled: the programme is brand-safe but the locally adaptable band and positioning weren't strong enough to lift demand to 120. Relevance, not just consistency, fills the seats.`,
                    insight_exemplary:      `Exemplary architecture: high coherence, break-even enrolment and sustainable faculty together. This is one coherent global programme that scales — and a portfolio decision made at the portfolio level.`,

                    hint_budget:            `You're over the €2.4M launch cap. Revisit the International Week format — the full-residential week alone is €480K — and the faculty mix before the economics break.`,
                    hint_burnout:           `Faculty utilization is in the burnout zone. Shift load off your six core faculty with hiring, visiting professors or online delivery, or you'll lose them and the quality with them.`,
                    hint_overstd:           `Coherence is very high but enrolment is lagging — you may be over-standardizing. Give the locally adaptable band more room so the distinct markets stay relevant.`,
                    hint_coherence:         `Coherence is well below the 75 floor. Strengthen the shared core and a common assessment spine, or the accreditors won't see one programme across the campuses.`,
                    hint_enrolment:         `Enrolment is short of break-even. Sharpen local relevance and positioning across the lead campuses — and check you've accounted for cannibalization of the existing portfolio.`,
                    hint_strong:            `Strong position — coherence, enrolment and utilization all healthy. Now lock in the evidence-led accreditation case and a staged roadmap so it survives the review.`,

